  "concreteGaps": [
    {
      "finding": "Both-host declaration is required, but actual unchanged upstream EventStore Program calls no actor qualification registration and offers no snapshot qualification configuration/discovery callback. Only code-level IServiceCollection registration exists; actor registration intentionally requires no Tenants state assembly.",
      "id": "actor-host-enrollment",
      "requiredDecision": "Authorize an upstream-owned supported deployment enrollment seam/release with the corresponding approved source-graph refresh, or explicitly renegotiate the immutable pinned-host/source-boundary constraint. No such authorization or implementation is inferred.",
      "scopeConflict": "The approved composition launches that gitlink-pinned upstream executable unchanged. Adding registry only to the cohosted benchmark fixture does not enroll the actual production actor host. Startup-hook/code injection, linked test code or a new copied gateway host would invent an unapproved extension/topology."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Actual keyed tenants processor is TenantAggregate : EventStoreAggregate<TenantState>; it retains normal async command and admitted/async replay interfaces but does not implement IAsyncFoldedSnapshotProcessor. DomainProcessorBase<TState> supplies capture, but lacks those aggregate replay interfaces and convention discovery scans EventStoreAggregate<TState>.",
      "id": "domain-processor-contract",
      "implication": "Adding a declaration cannot enable capture. A supported typed-processor adaptation or upstream aggregate capability must preserve existing discovery, all replay routes and real command behavior; a blind base-class replacement cannot be treated as equivalent."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Actual domain-service SDK registration has no bounded V1 producer for tenants. Router requires the bounded producer, matching typed qualification and IsQualified before ProcessForSnapshotAsync.",
      "id": "bounded-wire-producer",
      "implication": "All supported canonical tenant events/rejections need finite actual serializers and admitted output/scratch/representation limits; a registry entry alone is insufficient."
    }
  ],
